  "rule_description": "An external auto-closeable resource is acquired at this line: a java.io file stream/reader/writer, a java.net socket, a java.util.zip / java.util.jar archive, or a java.sql Statement/ResultSet. Pre-Java-7 code has to release it itself with an explicit close(), normally in a finally block, or it leaks; Java 7 try-with-resources closes it automatically when the block exits. The pattern flags the acquisition site - the line a conversion has to move into the try header - whether the resource is bound to a local variable or created inline as a call argument. In-memory streams (ByteArrayInputStream/OutputStream, StringReader/Writer), whose close() is a documented no-op and which are never a try-with-resources target, are deliberately excluded, as are cached java.sql PreparedStatement fields. An acquisition whose resource is stored in a field, and therefore deliberately outlives the method, is NOT this construct.",
  "rule_id": "TRY_WITH_RESOURCES",
  "rule_name": "Java 7 try-with-resources — manually released external resource",
